   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In 1633, an old astronomer was made to kneel and take back what his telescope had shown him: that the Earth moves around the Sun."
    },
    {
     "text": "His judges weren't being cruel for fun. They believed the idea was dangerous, that it could unsettle ordinary people and shake their faith."
    },
    {
     "text": "In other words, they were protecting people from a fact."
    },
    {
     "text": "",
     "dur": 1.4,
     "sfx": "whoosh"
    }
   ]
