    {
     "id": "q",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 620,
     "text": "Is he right? When is silence wise?",
     "color": "#c792ea",
     "d": 0.4,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In chapter two of Suicidal Empathy, the evolutionary psychologist Gad Saad argues that we still do this. Only now, the reason given is kindness."
    },
    {
     "text": "He calls it epistemological empathy: the urge to bury a finding, or soften a word, because the truth might hurt someone."
    },
    {
     "text": "Is he right? And when is holding back a fact actually wise?"
    }
   ]
