     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 560,
     "text": "not fear of heresy, fear of harm",
     "color": "#ff5a7a",
     "d": 2.6,
     "size": 20,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Every society has questions it would rather not ask. Saad calls the answers forbidden knowledge."
    },
    {
     "text": "Some of it is ancient. Spinoza was cast out of his community for his ideas about God. Galileo spent his last years under house arrest."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad's claim is that today's taboos are guarded by a newer emotion. Not fear of heresy, but fear of causing harm."
    }
   ]
  },
