     "in": 1
    },
    {
     "id": "fc2",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 630,
     "text": "judging a fact by its possible misuse, not by whether it is true",
     "size": 22,
     "d": 2.4,
     "color": "#c9d3ff",
     "weight": 700,
     "in": 1
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The logic goes like this. If a finding could be misused, and misuse would hurt people, then the finding itself must be harmful."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad calls this faulty consequentialism. You judge a fact by what someone might do with it, not by whether it's true."
    },
    {
     "text": "And once that rule is in place, almost anything can be ruled out of bounds."
    }
   ]
  },
