    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad's first case is the Harvard economist Roland Fryer, who in 2016 studied how police use force."
    },
    {
     "text": "He found racial gaps in lower-level force, like handcuffing and pushing people to the ground. But in the data he examined, he found no racial gap in police shootings."
    },
    {
     "text": "That second result was not what many people wanted to hear, and Fryer has said he received threats."
    },
    {
     "text": "In 2019, Harvard suspended him. The university said it was over complaints about his conduct toward staff, and that's the official record. Saad believes his research made him a target. Both accounts are public, so you can weigh them yourself."
    }
   ]
