   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The same instinct reshapes language. Institutions keep swapping plain words for gentler ones."
    },
    {
     "text": "A prisoner becomes a justice-involved individual. Obese becomes living in a larger body."
    },
    {
     "text": "Supporters say words can wound, and dignity matters. Saad says a softer label can hide a hard reality, and you can't fix what you won't name."
    }
   ]
