   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "His sharpest example is the body positivity slogan, healthy at any size."
    },
    {
     "text": "Fighting shame is reasonable. Shame doesn't help people get healthier, and stigma carries its own health costs."
    },
    {
     "text": "But large studies link obesity to diabetes, heart disease, and several cancers. Kindness that skips that part, Saad argues, isn't kindness at all."
    }
   ]
