    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad's next case is homelessness in big American cities, where tents line some streets for blocks."
    },
    {
     "text": "He borrows a phrase that the writer Michael Shellenberger applied to it: pathological altruism. Help that feels generous, but enables addiction and disorder."
    },
    {
     "text": "Supporters of Housing First, the policy of giving people homes without preconditions, point to studies showing that more people stay housed."
    },
    {
     "text": "Critics answer that housing alone does little for addiction or severe mental illness. Nearly everyone agrees that what many cities are doing now isn't working."
    }
