     "y": 380,
     "text": "not mockery: a warning",
     "color": "#5ec8e5",
     "d": 1.0,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad pairs the fable with a true story. In 2018, a young American couple cycling around the world wrote that evil was a make-believe concept, and that people are overwhelmingly kind."
    },
    {
     "text": "Days later, in Tajikistan, they and two other cyclists were run down and killed by attackers who had pledged loyalty to the Islamic State."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad stresses that he isn't mocking them. His point is that assuming the best about everyone can be a fatal mistake, because the world doesn't always return the favour."
    }
