   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now, the other side."
    },
    {
     "text": "Some caution about knowledge is wise. Scientists do withhold recipes for weapons, and research ethics exist for good reasons."
    },
    {
     "text": "Language does change, and a new word isn't always censorship. Sometimes it's simply courtesy."
    },
    {
     "text": "And Saad's own examples are disputed. Harvard says Fryer's case was about conduct, and Housing First has real evidence behind it."
    },
    {
     "text": "Where both sides can meet: a fact doesn't become false because it's uncomfortable. You can be gentle in how you say something, without changing what's true."
    }
   ]
